    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on exploiting favorable pitching matchups to stabilize our core counting categories. **Gunnar Henderson** (80.05) stands as our premier play, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against Melton and a favorable wind forecast that boosts his power profile. Following closely is **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). Both hitters draw exploitable matchups against Lorenzen and Bieber, respectively; the combination of high-scoring SP_xERA figures for these opposing pitchers and significant platoon advantages for our bats creates an elite environment for both to contribute heavily to our R and RBI totals. **Nasim Nunez** (63.70) remains a high-value start specifically for his speed profile, as his sprint-reliant output provides the necessary floor in our scarcest category despite a lower batting order slot.\n\nThe decision to bench **Coby Mayo** (46.72) was the most difficult call of the morning, as he missed the cut by less than a quarter-point relative to **Liam Hicks** (46.75). While **Coby Mayo** possesses intriguing power upside, the optimizer favored **Liam Hicks** due to the specific platoon dynamics against Nola. We are keeping a close watch on the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jacob Wilson**, **Curtis Mead**, **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Jackson Merrill**; should any of these bats be shuffled down the order, we will need to re-evaluate their efficiency scores to protect our remaining daily game caps. While **Sam Antonacci** draws a challenging assignment against Cole, his role at the top of the lineup maintains his start viability, though he carries the highest risk of underperformance given the superior arm he faces today.",
